  "query_preview": "..\nWidespread cirrus is covering the Marianas from remnants of this\nmornings thunderstorms over Tinian and Saipan. Weak, isolated showers\nremain this afternoon but are expected to ramp back up slightly\novernight as proximity to Invest 92W is producing an unstable \natmosphere. Therefore, scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms \nare in the forecast for tonight through tomorrow. Shower coverage is \nexpected to increase Thursday night through Friday as Invest 92W \npasses over the Marianas, bringing the potential for heavy rainfall \nand gusty winds with any thunderstorms that develop. As discussed in \nthe Tropical Systems section below, Invest 92W remains unlikely to \npass through the Marianas as a tropical storm. However, the Marianas \nshould still expect increasing showers, isolated thunderstorms, \nbuilding seas and surf, and stronger winds. Afterwards, a ridge of \nhigh pressure will fill in once 92W passes, bringing drier conditions\nto the Marianas.",
